## Conventions

- API responses: `{ success: boolean, message: string, data?: any }`; the frontend throws on `success === false`.
- Backend dates: `dd/MM/yyyy` or `dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm`.
- IDs: `'PREFIX-' + new Date().getTime()`.
- Booleans stored as text `'TRUE'`/`'FALSE'`; comparisons use `String(v).toUpperCase() === 'TRUE'`.
- Default admin seeded by `setupDatabase()`: `admin`/`admin123` (or SHA-256 hashed); `doLogin` has a fallback when the admin sheet is empty.
- `__BACKEND_FILE__` uses `const`/`let`; follow existing style in the file you edit.
